        "title": {
          "en": "A short story"
        },
        "text": {
          "en": "Meena's grandmother told her about Tamil poets who lived long ago.\n\"They wrote in the Sangam age,\" she said."
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "explain",
        "type": "explanation",
        "provenance": "original",
        "keepEnglishTerms": [
          "Sangam",
          "Chera",
          "Pandya"
        ],
        "text": {
          "en": "The Sangam age in South India lasted roughly from 300 BCE to 300 CE. Poets gathered in assemblies called sangams to write poems in Tamil.\nThe Cheras, Cholas and Pandyas were the three major kingdoms. Trade with Rome flourished through ports like Muziris and Puhar.\nTamil Sangam literature includes Tolkappiyam, Ettuthokai and Pattuppattu."
        }
      },
